# NO `demo Drag` HERE, DELIBERATELY.
#
# Tutorial 1's first task is "drag the file icon in", and CODAP v3.1.0 cannot
# complete a url drop at all — measured on stock codap3.concord.org with no
# proxy and no wrapper: the Importer plugin launches, its handshake with CODAP
# times out, and no dataset ever arrives. So the plugin now imports the data at
# startup and ticks that box before the student sees it (DOT-FORK 9 in
# onboarding.js).
#
# With the task already done, a live demonstration would import a SECOND copy of
# Mammals. Leaving the script out instead makes `__demo.run('tutorial1','Drag')`
# fail to resolve, and the plugin falls back to the canned MP4 — which shows
# what dragging a csv looks like without touching the document. That fallback is
# the floor the fork was built on (DOT-FORK 5/5); this leans on it on purpose.

demo MakeGraph
  say !
  goto toolbar:graph
  peer toolbar:graph
  tap toolbar:graph
  wait component:graph 30s
  beat 1.4
  revert
  say ?

demo MoveComponent
  say !
  peer titleBar:graph
  drag titleBar:graph -> workspace teaching
  wait componentMoved 30s
  beat 1.4
  revert
  say ?

demo AssignAttribute
  say !
  peer pill:Mass
  drag pill:Mass -> axisDrop:bottom teaching
  wait graphX:Mass 30s
  beat 1.6
  revert
  say ?

demo SecondAttribute
  say !
  peer pill:Sleep
  drag pill:Sleep -> axisDrop:left teaching
  wait graphY:Sleep 30s
  beat 1.6
  revert
  say ?
